From 0a555909cca47f26768824d7d43d577b4471b6b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ws07 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:01:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Web client (S1): what happened while away, from the
 records; S1 losses as notices
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Connection patch of workstream 07 (player experience), claim 3 and brief
item 1.

The page's first look was never news (hud/feed.mjs: "A first snapshot (prev
null) is not news"), and no S1 record became a notice: a caravan raided or
lost, a storehouse or structure seized, a siege declared on the viewer's
village, a vote of the nation decided. On an S1 season the first look now
tells, from the chronicle the page has read, what happened since the
player's own "seen" mark on this device (hud/returnsum.mjs, the workstream's
model; hud/returnwords.mjs its words): a head notice that says what it
covers — since the mark, or a stated window on a first visit, another
device, another wallet or a new season — and names a gap in what was read
without filling it, then one notice per item. "Seen" moves the mark;
closing does not. Between two looks the S1 records read since the last
tick become notices. Nothing is told that no record logged.

